WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.575
This example shows how population filtering and CASE
classification work together The

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.638
rule concerns completed stays so the WHERE clause
first removes admissions with

00:00:09.662 --> 00:00:14.188
no discharge date That prevents an ongoing stay from
being forced into

00:00:14.212 --> 00:00:19.688
a category that requires a completed duration
PostgreSQL can subtract one date

00:00:19.712 --> 00:00:23.962
from another and return the number of days CASE then
classifies the

00:00:23.988 --> 00:00:27.300
duration as Short for fewer than five days Medium
for five through

00:00:27.325 --> 00:00:31.562
ten days and Long for anything greater than ten Run
the query

00:00:31.588 --> 00:00:37.038
and inspect the boundary values A five-day stay
should be Medium The

00:00:37.062 --> 00:00:41.200
broader lesson is to define the population before
applying a classification rule
